A||||5||thecage||rough idle||||1||
Z||000000||thecage||11-14-2001||10:51 PM||||Can anyone help. 86gt with rough idle. What sould I check. The car was idling at about 900rpm with some movement. Now it's at 900 but will dip to 500-600 and jump up to 1000-1100 before going back to 900 and repeating the process all over again. I did replace the ignition module and ignition pick up coil in the distributer. I also replaced the ignition coil. Could anything I have done caused this problem. I did mark the distributer before I took it out and aligned the marks when I put it back in. My question is could it still be off alittle and should I play with the distributer.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ITB 2M4||11-14-2001||11:09 PM||||The 2.8 V-6 in my Z-24 Cavalier had to have the Idle Air Control solenoid replaced 4 times in the 187,000miles I drove it.  It did exactly what you are describing every time it would get worn.  The IAC bumps the idle up whenever the A/C compressor kicks in.  The actuator would get loose in the housing, and move to one side or another, allowing the idle to 'hunt' around.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000002||thecage||11-14-2001||11:16 PM||||anyone else have other suggestions||||reg||1
Z||000003||ray b||11-15-2001||01:07 AM||||wd-40 on wire conecter plugs can fix idle on the tps a very cheap fix and a good first try<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||11-15-2001||01:14 AM||||I am assuming that by replacing the parts you mentioned that you resolved the other problem and are now left with just a rough idle? (I wasn't clear on that) -- If you had the distributor out it is possible that the timing is off slightly but it sounds more like a mis-fire to me -- check and see that the proper plugs are wired to the proper contacts on the distributor. Beginning with #1 and going clockwise to #6........<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||thecage||11-16-2001||09:29 PM||||Well just an apdate on the hunting idle. My suspisions were correct. The timing was way off after I replaced the ignition module and ignition pickup coil. Yes I did mark it before I took it out and had it lined up again but still it was way off. Reset timing and now purrs like a cat.||||reg||1
